From ddfc4a81a392ac3cc31a6d8b119f0ff22ea57705 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Floyd <git@notmy.space>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 16:08:58 +0000
Subject: camss: Drive the focus lens and iris from the soft IPA

The soft IPA reports focus lens and iris controls alongside the sensor
controls, and takes their control maps at init() and configure() so that
it only offers LensPosition and the aperture when the sensor has them.
The simple pipeline handles them; the camss pipeline handler, which
replaces it for CAMSS, did not.

Pass the maps from both ISP backends (a helper collects the sensor, lens
and iris maps, which needs a non-const CameraSensor as the lens accessors
are non-const), apply lens and iris controls directly as they are separate
sub-devices outside the delayed controls, and park the focus lens at stop
with the same ramp as the simple pipeline, so that a VCM does not hold
coil current between captures or click onto its end stop.

Signed-off-by: William Floyd <git@notmy.space>
